# Build output. Not anchored to the root: a stray `cargo build` inside a crate
# directory makes its own target/, and that should not be committable either.
target/

# Scratch git worktrees. They live inside the repo, so without this they show up
# as untracked in the main checkout.
/.claude/worktrees/

**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
.DS_Store
/.idea
/.vscode
*.snap.new

# The docs website in website/. `node_modules/` is not anchored for the same
# reason target/ above is not: pnpm creates one wherever it is run, and none of
# them is committable. `website/pnpm-lock.yaml` is deliberately absent from this
# list — the lockfile is what makes a docs build reproducible, so it is tracked.
node_modules/

# Astro's build output and its generated-types cache. website/ is where both
# land today, since that is the directory holding astro.config.ts; the bare
# `.astro/` is the catch-all for the same command run from somewhere else.
website/dist/
website/.astro/
.astro/
